
Plans a research strategy, searches the web, reads sources, cross-checks facts, and produces a cited report.
Demonstrates: planning, tool use, citation handling, self-critique loops.

Architecture
plan → search → read/extract → synthesize → self-critique → revise
Stack: Python, an LLM API (function calling), a search tool (Tavily/Serper/web scraping), simple orchestration (LangGraph, or just hand-rolled loop — hand-rolled is actually more impressive since it proves you understand the mechanics, not just a framework)

